{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130203-how-do-you-narrate-the-physical-effects-of-fate-spells","id":1130203,"title":"How do you narrate the physical effects of Fate spells?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-17T04:24:27-07:00","id":1130203,"title":"How do you narrate the physical effects of Fate spells?","content":"Apologies if this has come up a bunch already! <br /> <br /> A couple of players are starting to toy with Fate more, particularly the various means of hexing someone, and while I am perfectly happy in my understanding of the mechanics of these effects I am a little unsure of how to narrate them as a GM. Here's a couple of examples of what I am talking about.<br /> <br /> 1. Liz the Acanthus is on the tube and some guy bumps into her. Liz has had a bad day and hexes the chap, inflicting the blindness condition. How exactly does the blindness occur?<br /> A) Another person in same carriage slips and throws his starbucks into the air, hot coffee splashes all over guys face, scalding and blinding him. <br /> B) As the curse takes hold, the mans vision darkens and he is spontaneously struck blind, with no apparent cause. <br /> <br /> 2. Liz is hunting down a pair of villainous Sleepers who abused her prior to her Awakening. In a murderous rage she casts Share Fate, binding the two Sleepers together. She proceeds to coldly put a bullet in Sleeper A's forehead. Sleeper B dies, but how exactly?<br /> A) He simply collapses, an identical bullet-hole in his head, but with no apparent bullet.<br /> B) Fate orchestrates his death, using whatever is convenient. A heart attack, a car accident, choking on a feather, etc. <br /> C) Fate orchestrates his death, but somehow the death of Sleeper B mirrors Sleeper A. A gun misfires, or a stray bullet flies through a wall into his forehead. <br /> <br /> I suspect the answer might be 'Whichever you think is the most cool, or fits the practitioners magical style' but I would still like to canvass you all on your personal approaches to this question. In gameplay terms it could make a significant difference in whether certain effects provoke disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T05:19:03-07:00","id":1130214,"title":"","content":"It can go either way really, Fate controls probability, and there is a chance that coffee goes flying into your face or your eyes suddenly failing.<br /> <br /> I know that Shared Fate was a spell that Dave spoiled on another forum and he decided &quot;it isn't obvious (when cast)&quot; so it would seem that the guy who died from it definitely did so in an obviously magical way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T10:14:31-07:00","id":1130338,"title":"","content":"Well i think you answered your own questions in the last paragraph, but Fate is the subtle arcana of Arcadia so its well, more subtle then Time at least. But yeah, magic and especially Fate can at times be hard to conceive around, how does it work. I'm on the same page as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> here i think, Fate finds a way. Either through small things like freak accidents or through playing the probability-game, whatever feels right in the time. If it's chance that some accident happen to fill the gap or just good luck to find the right book at the start of the library-search, it could be Fate.<br /> Fate can, if there it's reasonable, be the proverbial falling anvil IMHO. The spell however doesn't create the circumstance, the chance must be there from the start, or else the spell finds another probable way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 08-17-2017, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}